\details{
In a reporting tree, periods nest: any two periods
either do not overlap, or one contains the other.
Reporting trees arise, for instance, in
census tables of year of arrival, where most records have detailed periods (\code{"2015-2020"}), some have only broad periods (\code{"<2010"}), and some have no period at all (\code{"Missing"}).

Levels are ordered as follows:
\enumerate{
\item Leaves, that is, periods that contain no other period,
ordered by lower limit.
\item Broader periods, ordered so that each period comes
after all periods inside it, and before any period
entirely above it.
\item Labels that could not be interpreted, if \code{interpret_fail}
is \code{"warn"} or \code{"silent"}.
\item Labels for missing values, as defined by \code{\link[=period_is_missing]{period_is_missing()}}.
